{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"Two source-level questions are worth retaining. Commit advancement through append replies releases queued reads, while advancement through a configuration change does not make that call. Separately, the README allows same-batch persistence and message sending to overlap, while the `Ready` interface requires entries to be stored first. Neither establishes a defect yet; legal history, alternative completion paths, and contract applicability remain to be checked.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"/usr/bin/python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nsources=[]\ndef add(i,f,a,b,k='code_observation'): sources.append(dict(id=i,file=f,start_line=a,end_line=b,kind=k))\nadd('s-readme-caller','README.md',114,148,'document_statement')\nadd('s-ready-contract','node.go',49,113,'interface_statement')\nadd('s-async-contract','raft.go',155,194,'interface_statement')\nadd('s-durable-send','raft.go',512,600)\nadd('s-reset-authority','raft.go',775,813)\nadd('s-leadership','raft.go',891,993)\nadd('s-term-dispatch','raft.go',1085,1262)\nadd('s-proposal-read-admission','raft.go',1286,1368)\nadd('s-ack-commit','raft.go',1507,1575)\nadd('s-config-commit','raft.go',1975,2031)\nadd('s-release-reads','raft.go',2123,2160)\nadd('s-ready-output','rawnode.go',118,190)\nadd('s-storage-response','rawnode.go',225,366)\nadd('s-ready-completion','rawnode.go',405,494)\nadd('s-read-correlation','read_only.go',18,120)\nx=dict(action='research',rationale='Retain initial source-backed backbone observations and two discrepancies before completing the both-core map. No obligation or violation is inferred.',sources=sources,feedback=dict(ref_ids=['surface:raft.switchToConfig','surface:raft.stepLeader','surface:Ready','s-config-commit','s-ack-commit','s-release-reads','s-readme-caller','s-ready-contract','s-async-contract','s-durable-send','s-reset-authority','s-leadership','s-term-dispatch','s-proposal-read-admission','s-ready-output','s-storage-response','s-ready-completion','s-read-correlation'],answered='Initial A1/A2 connection: leader append replies update tracked match and may advance the commit index, while maybeCommit checks the current term through raftLog and the tracker. send routes append and vote responses through msgsAfterAppend; RawNode transfers those responses to storage completion messages or the synchronous Ready/Advance path. Thus persistence completion qualifies support before its consumer counts it. Authority transitions reset votes, replication progress and readOnly state; term dispatch rejects old responses, with an explicit exception allowing completed snapshots from old storage messages while refusing to stabilize their appended entries. These are implementation observations, not a complete correctness argument. Two sourced unresolved surfaces are retained: (1) stepLeader releases pendingReadIndexMessages when MsgAppResp advances commit, whereas switchToConfig can advance commit and broadcasts without that release. The queue is populated when a multi-voter leader has no current-term committed entry. A legal history reaching configuration-driven first current-term commit, and whether a later independent path guarantees release, remain unknown. (2) README caller instructions permit sending messages while same-batch entries persist, but Ready.Entries and Ready.Messages require storing entries before messages. The synchronous RawNode path places external msgsAfterAppend into Ready.Messages. This is a document/interface conflict to investigate, not permission to choose the weaker policy for a finding.',remaining=['Complete the both-core overview by reading election support aggregation, tracker/joint quorum logic, log matching and commit guards, configuration application and recovery, and Node caller/completion paths. Core readiness is not yet established.','Trace configuration-driven first current-term commitment through legal membership histories and pending-read producers/consumers before selecting a formal question. Determine whether the omitted release is reachable and whether bounded completion is actually owed.','Resolve synchronous caller ordering expectations against doc.go, Node interfaces and examples; distinguish incorrect usage under the stricter interface from an applicable implementation responsibility.','Inspect pendingReadIndexMessages across authority transitions separately from readOnly state: reset clears the latter but the displayed reset does not clear the former. Retention may be intentional and needs consumer-context reasoning.'],understanding='updated',rationale='These acquired ranges distinguish qualified support, authority invalidation, queued work and caller completion. Saving the local anomalies now prevents a later map from incorrectly making read release an unconditional effect of commit advancement. No execution has been performed and no formal Candidate is selected.'))\njson.dump(x,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-03_09-49-03-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
